Inspect validated Cue JSON, SubRip, or WebVTT as a privacy-bounded structural report.

Usage:
  cueson [global options] inspect [options] INPUT

Options:
  --format FORMAT  Select auto, cueson, srt, or vtt (default auto).
  --encoding NAME  Select the native source text encoding.
  --json           Write the compact inspection report version 1 as JSON.

Global options:
  -q, --quiet  Suppress informational and success diagnostics.
  --silent     Suppress every non-error diagnostic.
  --no-color   Disable diagnostic color.
  -h, --help   Show help.
  --           End option processing; following paths and operands remain literal.

Notes:
  Format aliases: json and cue-json for cueson; subrip for srt; webvtt for vtt.
  Encoding aliases: utf8; utf-8-bom, utf8-bom, utf-8-sig; utf16le, utf-16-le; utf16be, utf-16-be; windows1252, cp1252; iso8859-1, latin1, latin-1.
  Cue JSON prohibits --encoding. WebVTT accepts UTF-8 only.

Streams:
  stdout  One human report, or one compact JSON object with --json.
  stderr  Ordered source warnings and errors allowed by the global filters.

Exit codes:
  0  Command or explicit help completed successfully; warnings may be present.
  1  An accepted operation failed during processing, cancellation, or runtime I/O.
  2  Command syntax, an operand, an option, or a pre-execution requirement was invalid.

Examples:
  cueson inspect document.cueson.json
  cueson inspect --json captions.vtt
